1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,759
Today, the park. Our picnic is going farther
than the backyard.

2
00:00:04,909 --> 00:00:08,208
Excellent. I shall lead lunch to its
destination.

3
00:00:08,358 --> 00:00:10,448
Lunch would appreciate a map.

4
00:00:10,598 --> 00:00:14,300
It would also appreciate arriving before we
get hungry.

5
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,090
Six plates. Six napkins.

6
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:19,960
And a bag for our wrappers.

7
00:00:20,110 --> 00:00:22,830
The blanket gets to travel too.

8
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:27,460
Roll it tight, Max. It has a long walk today.

9
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:33,650
Past the fountain, right toward the big oak.

10
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,784
The bench under the oak. Got it.

11
00:00:36,934 --> 00:00:39,919
A bench. I can recognize a bench.

12
00:00:40,069 --> 00:00:44,300
Dad, remember the tree part. The park has
other benches.

13
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:47,530
There are two green benches.

14
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,960
This one has a squirrel.

15
00:00:50,110 --> 00:00:54,150
Then we shall choose the one with our family.

16
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:58,780
Does the squirrel get a sandwich if we choose
wrong?

17
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:02,970
Sandwiches stay cool until we eat.

18
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:04,520
Blanket with me.

19
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:08,270
Plates with Dad. Nobody has to carry
everything.

20
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:12,900
Good. We can share the carrying as well as
lunch.

21
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:19,481
I have the basket and a remarkable sense of
direction.

22
00:01:19,631 --> 00:01:21,369
Which direction is remarkable?

23
00:01:21,519 --> 00:01:24,919
We can check that when we get there.

24
00:01:25,069 --> 00:01:29,300
The direction that gets these plates to lunch,
I hope.

25
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:31,210
Everybody ready?

26
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:34,520
Ready for the bench with the people.

27
00:01:34,670 --> 00:01:38,270
Stay beside us. We will find it together.

28
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:43,340
I'll look for the big oak when we reach the
gate.

29
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:48,410
Such a small tree. Easy to spot.

30
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:50,840
It is a drawing, Dad.

31
00:01:50,990 --> 00:01:54,150
The real one may be slightly taller.

32
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:58,780
Good. We won't have to eat under a pencil
mark.

33
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:02,090
There is the fountain.

34
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:04,960
And the big oak beyond it.

35
00:02:05,110 --> 00:02:09,150
I recognize at least three things from the
map.

36
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:13,780
Can you match them to the drawing from here,
Dad?

37
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:19,186
Our place is under that oak, on the right.

38
00:02:19,336 --> 00:02:22,414
The squirrel is on the other side.

39
00:02:22,564 --> 00:02:24,786
A useful neighbor to remember.

40
00:02:24,936 --> 00:02:29,300
If he looks like a squirrel, we've gone too
far.

41
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:33,757
We will spread the blanket under the oak.

42
00:02:33,907 --> 00:02:36,986
We will be right across the fountain.

43
00:02:37,136 --> 00:02:39,786
We will follow with the plates.

44
00:02:39,936 --> 00:02:44,300
Just look for us when you come round the
fountain.

45
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:47,090
Right at the fountain.

46
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:49,960
Yes. We can still see Dad.

47
00:02:50,110 --> 00:02:53,270
He has only the plates to persuade.

48
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:57,460
They'd better come. Lunch needs something to
land on.

49
00:03:00,250 --> 00:03:02,530
There. Tree on the left.

50
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,960
I thought Mom said right.

51
00:03:05,110 --> 00:03:08,270
Let us compare it with the scenery.

52
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:12,460
Dad, the trees on paper look funny from here.

53
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:17,090
That bench is green.

54
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:18,640
An excellent match.

55
00:03:18,790 --> 00:03:20,630
What about the tree?

56
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:24,820
Fair question. Nobody promised us the only
green bench.

57
00:03:24,970 --> 00:03:27,690
Shouldn't our tree be bigger, too?

58
00:03:30,250 --> 00:03:32,970
There is a tree beside it.

59
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:35,840
There are trees beside almost everything.

60
00:03:35,990 --> 00:03:38,710
This park has been very thorough.

61
00:03:38,860 --> 00:03:43,340
But only one of those trees is our big oak.

62
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:46,210
Destination reached.

63
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:50,840
The picnic seems to be missing most of the
picnic.

64
00:03:50,990 --> 00:03:52,390
Including our family.

65
00:03:52,540 --> 00:03:57,460
Ah. That's quite a lot for a picnic to be
missing.

66
00:04:00,250 --> 00:04:03,410
One, two, three. We ordered six people.

67
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:06,720
Perhaps the others are admiring the view.

68
00:04:06,870 --> 00:04:09,150
We should admire the directions.

69
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:13,340
I still count three. Nobody's hiding behind
you, Dad.

70
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:18,516
Excuse me. Have you seen our picnic?

71
00:04:18,666 --> 00:04:20,568
Our friend seems quiet.

72
00:04:20,718 --> 00:04:23,529
Stone squirrels are excellent at waiting.

73
00:04:23,679 --> 00:04:27,400
And apparently terrible at giving directions
out loud.

74
00:04:30,250 --> 00:04:32,152
There is no blanket.

75
00:04:32,302 --> 00:04:34,204
Mom Maya has it.

76
00:04:34,354 --> 00:04:38,074
A strong clue that lunch went somewhere else.

77
00:04:38,224 --> 00:04:42,400
Same green paint, though. I see why you
stopped.

78
00:04:45,250 --> 00:04:48,650
I can call them if we need help.

79
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:51,784
First, let us check where we are.

80
00:04:51,934 --> 00:04:54,919
Good. The bench is not going anywhere.

81
00:04:55,069 --> 00:04:59,300
Good point. The map might have an opinion on
this.

82
00:05:00,250 --> 00:05:02,607
There is another green bench.

83
00:05:02,757 --> 00:05:04,658
It has copied ours.

84
00:05:04,808 --> 00:05:08,074
Or ours copied the one with lunch.

85
00:05:08,224 --> 00:05:12,400
Worth checking which one's got the oak beside
it.

86
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:17,530
Our neighbor is a squirrel.

87
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:19,520
The drawing says oak.

88
00:05:19,670 --> 00:05:22,830
The bench had a very convincing alibi.

89
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:27,460
The squirrel hasn't got much to say in its
defense.

90
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:32,530
Dad, the arrow points down.

91
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:35,840
A south-going north arrow. That is unusual.

92
00:05:35,990 --> 00:05:38,710
Maybe the paper is upside down.

93
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:43,340
That would certainly save us from turning the
park around.

94
00:05:45,250 --> 00:05:47,970
That would explain the adventurous tree.

95
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:51,720
Gate at the bottom. Fountain in the middle.

96
00:05:51,870 --> 00:05:55,030
Now lunch is on the other side.

97
00:05:55,180 --> 00:05:59,220
So that's where we should be taking these
plates.

98
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:03,410
I saw a bench and stopped checking.

99
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:04,960
Easy to do.

100
00:06:05,110 --> 00:06:08,270
The squirrel was not much help either.

101
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:12,460
Actually, he's the part that gave this place
away.

102
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:16,650
Which bench, Dad?

103
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:19,960
The green bench under the big oak.

104
00:06:20,110 --> 00:06:23,710
That gives us something we can actually check.

105
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:28,340
And if we see the squirrel, we've already
checked him.

106
00:06:30,250 --> 00:06:33,061
We are beside the squirrel statue.

107
00:06:33,211 --> 00:06:36,023
So it did tell us something.

108
00:06:36,173 --> 00:06:38,074
Without saying a word.

109
00:06:38,224 --> 00:06:42,400
That's more help than I got from guessing
green.

110
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:49,066
Gate behind us, fountain ahead, squirrel to
the west.

111
00:06:49,216 --> 00:06:51,784
And our oak to the east.

112
00:06:51,934 --> 00:06:54,919
The paper and park are friends again.

113
00:06:55,069 --> 00:06:59,300
Let's keep them that way until we get to
lunch.

114
00:07:00,250 --> 00:07:03,410
Could we bring this bench to lunch?

115
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:06,280
It seems attached to the park.

116
00:07:06,430 --> 00:07:08,710
Moving us will be easier.

117
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:13,340
Fair point. The plates are lighter than a
whole bench.

118
00:07:15,250 --> 00:07:17,970
It looks closer across the flowers.

119
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:21,280
The path is the way for us.

120
00:07:21,430 --> 00:07:24,150
The flowers already have their seats.

121
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:28,340
Okay. We'll walk round and leave them to it.

122
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:33,791
There they are. They can see us.

123
00:07:33,941 --> 00:07:36,003
They have the blanket.

124
00:07:36,153 --> 00:07:38,216
And the better bench.

125
00:07:38,366 --> 00:07:42,400
Better company, too. No offense to our
squirrel.

126
00:07:45,250 --> 00:07:46,819
Nothing left behind.

127
00:07:46,969 --> 00:07:49,524
Except a confidently wrong conclusion.

128
00:07:49,674 --> 00:07:52,722
The squirrel can look after that.

129
00:07:52,872 --> 00:07:57,400
Come on, Dad. Lunch won't find us sitting
here.

130
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:03,757
Back to the fountain. Then we check again.

131
00:08:03,907 --> 00:08:06,986
A known place is a useful start.

132
00:08:07,136 --> 00:08:10,214
This time, we bring the north arrow.

133
00:08:10,364 --> 00:08:14,300
Good. I don't want another trip to the statue.

134
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:17,530
Gate behind us. Fountain ahead.

135
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:19,960
Now right, toward the oak.

136
00:08:20,110 --> 00:08:23,710
The real tree. Not the little upside-down one.

137
00:08:23,860 --> 00:08:27,900
It's easier to see now that we're facing it.

138
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:32,970
The fountain sounds different up close.

139
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:36,280
A good reason to stop and notice.

140
00:08:36,430 --> 00:08:39,590
And now we know where we are.

141
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:44,220
And we can hear it without looking at a map.

142
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:48,410
Right at the fountain, toward the oak.

143
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:51,280
And away from our stone adviser.

144
00:08:51,430 --> 00:08:54,590
He has done enough guiding for today.

145
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:58,780
At least we won't have to thank him twice.

146
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:02,805
That bench has our people.

147
00:09:02,955 --> 00:09:05,510
And a very promising lunch.

148
00:09:05,660 --> 00:09:07,229
Two excellent landmarks.

149
00:09:07,379 --> 00:09:12,400
And an oak. We can finally tick off all three.

150
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:17,530
We saved all six places.

151
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:20,400
Your plates took the scenic route.

152
00:09:20,550 --> 00:09:23,270
The sandwiches waited in the shade.

153
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:27,900
I hope the boys have an appetite after that
walk.

154
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:32,530
Six people. One correct bench.

155
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:34,960
And one family, all here.

156
00:09:35,110 --> 00:09:37,830
The map needed a little turning.

157
00:09:37,980 --> 00:09:42,460
All the way around, Dad. Tell them about the
arrow.

158
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:50,043
I held the map upside down and trusted the
first bench.

159
00:09:50,193 --> 00:09:51,986
That explains the detour.

160
00:09:52,136 --> 00:09:55,214
The statue helped us work it out.

161
00:09:55,364 --> 00:09:59,300
I owe that squirrel a thank-you. You two, too.

162
00:10:00,250 --> 00:10:03,410
A bench alone was not enough information.

163
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:07,160
Right at the fountain, under the big oak.

164
00:10:07,310 --> 00:10:09,150
Much harder to confuse.

165
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:13,340
Especially when the other bench has a stone
squirrel.

166
00:10:15,250 --> 00:10:18,329
I could have pointed out both benches.

167
00:10:18,479 --> 00:10:21,557
And I could have checked before walking.

168
00:10:21,707 --> 00:10:26,071
The bench was not the only thing needing a
partner.

169
00:10:26,221 --> 00:10:29,300
Next time let's point it out together.

170
00:10:30,250 --> 00:10:32,530
This sleeve keeps it dry.

171
00:10:32,680 --> 00:10:36,720
And I shall keep the top at the top.

172
00:10:36,870 --> 00:10:38,710
An ambitious new system.

173
00:10:38,860 --> 00:10:43,340
And we can see it without getting sandwich on
it.

174
00:10:45,250 --> 00:10:47,471
Can we open lunch now?

175
00:10:47,621 --> 00:10:51,128
After clean hands. The pavilion has a sink.

176
00:10:51,278 --> 00:10:54,786
I can see its red roof from here.

177
00:10:54,936 --> 00:10:59,300
Good. Even from here I can tell those roofs
apart.

178
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:02,970
We will take everything with us.

179
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:06,280
This time, I know the way back.

180
00:11:06,430 --> 00:11:08,710
The oak will wait too.

181
00:11:08,860 --> 00:11:12,900
Come on, then. Nobody needs to guard lunch
alone.

182
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:17,229
Same blanket, right place.

183
00:11:17,379 --> 00:11:19,357
A very satisfying combination.

184
00:11:19,507 --> 00:11:21,959
Now we can settle in.

185
00:11:22,109 --> 00:11:27,400
Let's leave a little room at the blanket edge
for me.

186
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:32,090
Everyone found a place.

187
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:37,160
The right bench only needed one attempt from
most of us.

188
00:11:37,310 --> 00:11:39,590
I enjoyed the extra research.

189
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:44,220
Did your research discover that sandwiches
taste better over here?

190
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:48,650
Would all of us fit on that bench?

191
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:51,369
We have more room right here.

192
00:11:51,519 --> 00:11:55,334
The bench helped us find a good place, too.

193
00:11:55,484 --> 00:11:59,300
Good. My knees were hoping for some blanket
space.

194
00:12:00,250 --> 00:12:03,061
One plate for each of us.

195
00:12:03,211 --> 00:12:04,204
Thank you.

196
00:12:04,354 --> 00:12:08,074
At last, the plates have met their passengers.

197
00:12:08,224 --> 00:12:12,400
They can put in for a rest after lunch.

198
00:12:15,250 --> 00:12:18,146
My napkin is on the right side.

199
00:12:18,296 --> 00:12:21,192
The useful side is beside your plate.

200
00:12:21,342 --> 00:12:25,044
You can put it wherever you can reach
comfortably.

201
00:12:25,194 --> 00:12:29,300
Beside my plate makes sense. My elbow can find
it.

202
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:33,516
Still cool. Six sandwiches, ready to share.

203
00:12:33,666 --> 00:12:36,023
Lunch followed its instructions perfectly.

204
00:12:36,173 --> 00:12:38,074
It had excellent transport.

205
00:12:38,224 --> 00:12:42,400
Let's hand them out while they're nice and
cool.

206
00:12:45,250 --> 00:12:47,229
Six plates, six sandwiches.

207
00:12:47,379 --> 00:12:48,884
Nobody left out.

208
00:12:49,034 --> 00:12:52,432
And no sandwich at the squirrel bench.

209
00:12:52,582 --> 00:12:57,400
I think the squirrel would just sit on his
anyway.

210
00:13:00,250 --> 00:13:01,650
One bottle each.

211
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:05,400
This water did not come from the fountain.

212
00:13:05,550 --> 00:13:09,590
Correct. It came all the way from our fridge.

213
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:14,220
Good. I prefer the kind that comes in a
bottle.

214
00:13:15,250 --> 00:13:17,530
Open it over your plate.

215
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:19,960
The wrapper wants to fly.

216
00:13:20,110 --> 00:13:22,830
Our pouch will keep it here.

217
00:13:22,980 --> 00:13:27,460
Got it. This wrapper isn't getting its own
park tour.

218
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:33,298
Worth finding the right place for.

219
00:13:33,448 --> 00:13:35,017
The shade helps.

220
00:13:35,167 --> 00:13:37,229
So does being together.

221
00:13:37,379 --> 00:13:42,400
The walk gave me quite an appetite for this
sandwich.

222
00:13:45,250 --> 00:13:48,410
The sun stopped at our blanket edge.

223
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:50,400
A very polite sun.

224
00:13:50,550 --> 00:13:53,710
The oak is doing the hard work.

225
00:13:53,860 --> 00:13:58,340
Can it keep doing that till I finish my lunch?

226
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:02,530
That bench looked exactly right.

227
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:05,840
Until we checked what was beside it.

228
00:14:05,990 --> 00:14:08,270
And interviewed its quietest neighbor.

229
00:14:08,420 --> 00:14:12,460
I never thought a statue could answer a
question.

230
00:14:15,250 --> 00:14:17,043
You helped one another.

231
00:14:17,193 --> 00:14:22,414
They let me turn the paper before turning me
into a joke.

232
00:14:22,564 --> 00:14:24,786
Only a very small joke.

233
00:14:24,936 --> 00:14:29,300
A small one is fair. I did ask a squirrel.

234
00:14:30,250 --> 00:14:32,471
Can a map hear directions?

235
00:14:32,621 --> 00:14:35,700
No. I have to do that part.

236
00:14:35,850 --> 00:14:40,214
A map is helpful company, not a replacement
for listening.

237
00:14:40,364 --> 00:14:44,300
I'll listen for the tree part first next time.

238
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:47,970
Best shade goes to the oak.

239
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:50,840
It has been practicing for years.

240
00:14:50,990 --> 00:14:54,150
And it already knows where to stand.

241
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:58,340
The tree definitely had the shortest trip to
lunch.

242
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:04,066
I wanted to take care of the directions
myself.

243
00:15:04,216 --> 00:15:08,031
You do not have to do every part alone.

244
00:15:08,181 --> 00:15:09,919
Helping can include asking.

245
00:15:10,069 --> 00:15:14,300
I like having two people around who notice
different things.

246
00:15:15,250 --> 00:15:19,290
Leo found the arrow. Max found the wrong
neighbor.

247
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,720
You carried all the plates.

248
00:15:21,870 --> 00:15:23,710
That was useful too.

249
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:27,900
Thanks. I thought I'd only contributed the
extra walk.

250
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:32,970
Was the real tree slightly taller?

251
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:35,840
An unexpectedly large amount of slightly.

252
00:15:35,990 --> 00:15:38,270
Fortunately, the shade is full-sized.

253
00:15:38,420 --> 00:15:42,900
Plenty of shade for someone with a very small
map.

254
00:15:45,250 --> 00:15:49,066
How would you tell us where this picnic is?

255
00:15:49,216 --> 00:15:52,616
Under the big oak, right of the fountain.

256
00:15:52,766 --> 00:15:54,919
I would find you easily.

257
00:15:55,069 --> 00:15:59,300
And if you see the squirrel, wave across at
us.

258
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:03,410
The fountain stayed exactly where it was.

259
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:05,400
Very considerate of it.

260
00:16:05,550 --> 00:16:08,270
The map was the busy one.

261
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:12,460
Funny how different it looked after just one
turn.

262
00:16:15,250 --> 00:16:17,805
That was a good lunch.

263
00:16:17,955 --> 00:16:21,003
And we kept everything with us.

264
00:16:21,153 --> 00:16:22,722
Especially the people.

265
00:16:22,872 --> 00:16:27,400
Let's check under the plates when we pack up.

266
00:16:30,250 --> 00:16:33,410
The basket can carry the plates home.

267
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:36,720
It has had a very educational journey.

268
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:39,150
And only one unnecessary stop.

269
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:43,780
I think the plates would prefer a direct trip
home.

270
00:16:45,250 --> 00:16:47,530
No wrappers on the grass.

271
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:50,400
Good. We take our things home.

272
00:16:50,550 --> 00:16:54,150
The next family should find clean shade too.

273
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:59,220
I want the next picnic to have a nice spot
too.

274
00:17:00,250 --> 00:17:03,410
The place looks different without the blanket.

275
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:05,400
Still the oak bench.

276
00:17:05,550 --> 00:17:08,710
Now we know it without our belongings.

277
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:13,340
That's how we'll find it next time, even
before lunch.

278
00:17:15,250 --> 00:17:17,970
Fountain first. Then the south gate.

279
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:20,840
A clear starting point and destination.

280
00:17:20,990 --> 00:17:23,270
No squirrel appointment this time.

281
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:28,340
This time the fountain's on our way out of the
park.

282
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:32,970
Keep this arrow at the top.

283
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:36,720
Top at the top. I remember the system.

284
00:17:36,870 --> 00:17:39,150
It seems to be working.

285
00:17:39,300 --> 00:17:43,340
Just remember to turn yourself when we turn
around.

286
00:17:45,250 --> 00:17:47,090
Thank you, quiet guide.

287
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:50,400
He helped us notice where we were.

288
00:17:50,550 --> 00:17:53,710
And we helped each other get here.

289
00:17:53,860 --> 00:17:58,340
I'll wave for him. His paws look busy staying
still.

290
00:18:00,250 --> 00:18:02,607
Which bench will you remember?

291
00:18:02,757 --> 00:18:06,477
Both. One for lunch, one for the story.

292
00:18:06,627 --> 00:18:08,074
A useful pair.

293
00:18:08,224 --> 00:18:12,400
I'll remember which one has the surprisingly
patient squirrel.

294
00:18:15,250 --> 00:18:16,650
Everybody with us?

295
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:17,650
Everybody.

296
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:19,640
Even the direction expert.

297
00:18:19,790 --> 00:18:24,270
Especially him. We want his version of the
story later.

298
00:18:24,420 --> 00:18:28,020
Somebody should give the squirrel a speaking
part.

299
00:18:30,250 --> 00:18:31,199
Any shortcuts?

300
00:18:31,349 --> 00:18:34,910
Only in my explanation. We are going home.

301
00:18:35,060 --> 00:18:36,444
Very clear directions.

302
00:18:36,594 --> 00:18:40,590
Good. Home is a landmark my feet already know.

303
00:18:40,740 --> 00:18:44,300
Good. Let's give those feet the last word.

304
00:18:45,250 --> 00:18:46,326
Home again.

305
00:18:46,476 --> 00:18:48,538
Everything back with us.

306
00:18:48,688 --> 00:18:52,229
And a much better understanding of benches.

307
00:18:52,379 --> 00:18:57,400
Next time the directions can travel with a
second reader.

308
00:19:00,250 --> 00:19:01,650
Blanket to laundry.

309
00:19:01,800 --> 00:19:03,640
Plates to the sink.

310
00:19:03,790 --> 00:19:05,630
People to somewhere comfortable?

311
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:10,260
After the basket's empty, your knees can clock
out too.

312
00:19:10,410 --> 00:19:13,130
Good. They've had quite a day.

313
00:19:15,250 --> 00:19:19,186
A place for the map. The right way up.

314
00:19:19,336 --> 00:19:21,128
Ready for next time.

315
00:19:21,278 --> 00:19:24,786
And next time, we can all check together.

316
00:19:24,936 --> 00:19:29,300
Deal. The park's big enough for more than one
navigator.

317
00:19:30,250 --> 00:19:33,329
We have our restaurant dinner another evening.

318
00:19:33,479 --> 00:19:37,414
I shall ask one clear question at a time.

319
00:19:37,564 --> 00:19:40,214
Will the menu need a map?

320
00:19:40,364 --> 00:19:44,300
Only if dessert is hiding behind a stone
squirrel.

321
00:19:45,250 --> 00:19:49,481
Next time, I will look for the bench with
everyone.

322
00:19:49,631 --> 00:19:52,200
We will leave you a place.

323
00:19:52,350 --> 00:19:54,503
The squirrel can keep his.

324
00:19:54,653 --> 00:19:59,300
We'll save you the shady spot, Dad. You earned
the walk.
